1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:02,350
AI Urban Flood Sentinel brings drain-inspection

2
00:00:02,537 --> 00:00:04,213
information into one dashboard.

3
00:00:04,978 --> 00:00:06,566
It helps teams review images and

4
00:00:06,616 --> 00:00:08,038
see why a record needs attention

5
00:00:08,088 --> 00:00:09,348
before the crew heads out.

6
00:00:09,436 --> 00:00:10,930
The top cards count records by

7
00:00:10,980 --> 00:00:13,498
category at a glance: critical, high,

8
00:00:13,548 --> 00:00:15,475
moderate, low, and needs inspection.

9
00:00:16,304 --> 00:00:18,255
That last group preserves uncertainty for

10
00:00:18,305 --> 00:00:19,256
human review.

11
00:00:19,859 --> 00:00:21,673
All seven starting records are synthetic

12
00:00:21,723 --> 00:00:23,804
examples, not a live city feed.

13
00:00:23,894 --> 00:00:25,726
To prepare an inspection, choose a

14
00:00:25,776 --> 00:00:27,254
drain photo or use a sample

15
00:00:27,304 --> 00:00:27,918
button.

16
00:00:28,473 --> 00:00:30,568
The blocked-drain sample fills the preview.

17
00:00:31,244 --> 00:00:32,543
Entering a drain ID lets the

18
00:00:32,593 --> 00:00:33,905
result join the queue.

19
00:00:34,428 --> 00:00:36,345
Location is optional, and the map

20
00:00:36,395 --> 00:00:37,395
can fill coordinates.

21
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:40,182
Rainfall is entered by the operator;

22
00:00:40,488 --> 00:00:41,970
confirm the value before analysis.

23
00:00:42,058 --> 00:00:44,484
Run analysis starts the selected-image workflow.

24
00:00:45,221 --> 00:00:46,771
This recording is in clearly marked

25
00:00:46,821 --> 00:00:48,698
mock mode, so its result comes

26
00:00:48,748 --> 00:00:50,734
from a synthetic fixture; no image

27
00:00:50,784 --> 00:00:51,528
is analysed.

28
00:00:52,317 --> 00:00:54,298
Normally, the backend sends the photo

29
00:00:54,348 --> 00:00:55,751
to a local vision model.

30
00:00:56,311 --> 00:00:57,880
If it cannot assess an image,

31
00:00:58,046 --> 00:01:00,281
the application reports an inconclusive result

32
00:01:00,331 --> 00:01:01,871
instead of calling the drain clear.

33
00:01:01,958 --> 00:01:03,186
Here the fixture shows a low

34
00:01:03,236 --> 00:01:05,223
score and a routine-inspection recommendation.

35
00:01:06,169 --> 00:01:07,862
Its blockage and rainfall values are

36
00:01:07,912 --> 00:01:10,049
synthetic, as the labels explain.

37
00:01:10,778 --> 00:01:12,673
In a real analysis, blockage is

38
00:01:12,723 --> 00:01:14,390
a rough visual estimate, not a

39
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:15,450
physical measurement.

40
00:01:16,163 --> 00:01:18,410
The experimental score combines inputs available

41
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:19,536
to the risk engine.

42
00:01:20,131 --> 00:01:21,322
It is not a probability of

43
00:01:21,372 --> 00:01:21,973
flooding.

44
00:01:22,583 --> 00:01:25,259
Historical vulnerability data is synthetic, and

45
00:01:25,309 --> 00:01:26,702
missing inputs are labelled for this

46
00:01:26,752 --> 00:01:27,090
example.

47
00:01:27,178 --> 00:01:28,912
The map shows drains with coordinates,

48
00:01:29,381 --> 00:01:30,921
using matching risk colours.

49
00:01:31,615 --> 00:01:33,886
Dashed rings identify synthetic locations.

50
00:01:34,757 --> 00:01:36,080
The queue groups critical and high

51
00:01:36,130 --> 00:01:38,637
records under Act first, unclear records

52
00:01:38,687 --> 00:01:41,064
under Needs manual inspection, then moderate

53
00:01:41,114 --> 00:01:42,529
and low records for scheduling.

54
00:01:43,327 --> 00:01:44,765
Selecting a queue row opens its

55
00:01:44,815 --> 00:01:47,290
details, recommendation, and data-source flags.

56
00:01:47,385 --> 00:01:49,693
The inconclusive example shows the safeguard

57
00:01:49,743 --> 00:01:52,324
in practice: no usable blockage estimate

58
00:01:52,374 --> 00:01:54,202
means no score, no alert, and

59
00:01:54,252 --> 00:01:56,058
a recommendation for manual inspection.

60
00:01:56,146 --> 00:01:57,512
The critical screen is another mock

61
00:01:57,562 --> 00:01:58,167
fixture.

62
00:01:58,864 --> 00:02:00,564
The alert appears because this fixture

63
00:02:00,614 --> 00:02:02,369
carries a critical backend level.

64
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:05,557
Its urgent-intervention recommendation shows the suggested

65
00:02:05,607 --> 00:02:06,212
response.

66
00:02:07,008 --> 00:02:09,385
These values are synthetic, not findings

67
00:02:09,435 --> 00:02:10,753
from the selected photograph.

68
00:02:11,617 --> 00:02:13,072
In a real run, the image

69
00:02:13,122 --> 00:02:14,754
model's assessment would contribute to the

70
00:02:14,804 --> 00:02:15,508
backend result.

71
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:17,559
AI Urban Flood Sentinel makes evidence

72
00:02:17,609 --> 00:02:19,634
easier to review and priorities easier

73
00:02:19,684 --> 00:02:20,428
to explain.

74
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:23,578
It supports decisions with assumptions visible.

75
00:02:24,229 --> 00:02:25,994
Teams can choose what to inspect.

76
00:02:26,765 --> 00:02:27,862
Smarter inspection.

77
00:02:28,709 --> 00:02:29,400
Clearer priorities.

